id: pm-gantt-chart-ugun
title: Fresh installs fail strict health because manifest.json carries an unsupported pm key
description: "A fresh pm 2026.8.17 project installs and activates pm-gantt-chart, but pm health --strict-exit returns ok:false with extension_manifest_unknown_key:project:pm-gantt-chart:key=pm. The public SDK compatibility checker reports the same manifest_unknown_key finding. Remove the ignored legacy compatibility block and gate the whole raw manifest through the SDK checker so future unknown keys fail in CI before release."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: activation,manifest,production-readiness,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-17T05:04:47.827Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T05:23:30.783Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T05:14:58.983Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T05:14:58.983Z"
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "The public SDK compatibility checker returns compatible:true with zero findings for the raw manifest at the package's pinned PM version; a fresh local install passes pm health --strict-exit; command and exporter still activate; removing the legacy key is covered by a test that failed before the fix"
risk: high
release: 2026.8.18
resolution: Removed the ignored legacy pm compatibility object and added an SDK compatibility test over the complete raw manifest at the exact pinned CLI version.
expected_result: The package manifest contains only supported extension keys and a fresh activated install passes strict health.
actual_result: The SDK checker returns compatible true with zero findings; fresh install activates and pm health --strict-exit passes with zero warnings.
